 * If you want to have an assertion that should be verified in the test execution when the PreCondition is not met,
 * do it in such following manner:
 *
 *  AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index < arrList.Count);
 *
 * Assertion
 * In the contract test you can use Debug.Assert() for verification:
 *
 * Assert.That(New_arrListIndexOfX_after_remove, Is.LessThanOrEqualTo(Old_arrListCount - 1));
